The derivation is structural rather than verbatim: no file in this repository is a
copy of an upstream source file, and long identical spans are limited to shared
idiom (imports, dataclass field lists, `subprocess.run` keyword arguments). The
following modules nevertheless follow the upstream design, API shape, and in places
substantially similar expression, and should be treated as derivative works:

  sdk/freewheel/ext4.py      e2fsprogs image wrapper; class/method layout and
                             helper decomposition follow nebi-patch's ext4 module
  sdk/freewheel/ota.py       OTA package verification and TUS upload; constants,
                             report dataclasses, and uploader shape follow
                             nebi-patch's validator/uploader modules
  sdk/freewheel/md_ts.py     MD-TS wire format, implemented from the byte-level
                             spec in the community cross-check note (§4)
  sdk/freewheel/transport.py UCP counter/SACK model aligned to the upstream one,
                             pinned by sdk/tests/test_crosscheck.py
  sdk/tests/crosscheck/      Test vectors generated by the upstream encoders

Frozen test vectors in sdk/tests/crosscheck/vectors.json are byte outputs of the
upstream encoders. They are retained as evidence of where the protocol constants
came from.

